---
/**
 * Fellowships: the two tracks side by side, then how a fellowship runs, as
 * numbered steps because it is a sequence.
 *
 * Copy follows Rohan's description of the plan (10 October 2026). Anything
 * not yet set up is written as a plan ("we plan to"), never as done.
 */
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
---
<section class="band band--river section" id="fellowships" aria-labelledby="fellowships-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="fellowships-title" class="section-title dot">Fellowships</h2>
    <p class="lede section-lede">
      An 8-week introduction to AI safety, taught by people who work on it. There are no AI safety
      courses for most Northeastern students, so we built one. Fellowships start in January 2027.
    </p>

    <h3 class="sub">Two tracks, one fellowship</h3>
    <div class="tracks">
      <article class="track">
        <Icon name="chip" tone="river" />
        <h4>Technical track</h4>
        <p class="track__for">For people who want to make AI systems safer by working on the systems themselves.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>How modern AI systems are trained</li>
          <li>Why aligning them is hard</li>
          <li>Mechanistic interpretability: looking inside a model</li>
          <li>Technical governance</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="track__need">Starts from the fundamentals.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="track">
        <Icon name="policy" tone="sun" />
        <h4>Policy track</h4>
        <p class="track__for">For people who want to shape the rules around AI.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>The risks posed by advanced AI</li>
          <li>How governments and companies are responding</li>
          <li>What good standards, safeguards and laws could look like</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="track__need">No technical background needed.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="note note--plain">
      Both tracks lead to the same place. Finish either one and you are a fellow; the track is
      only your focus.
    </p>

    <h3 class="sub">How it works</h3>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li>
        <h4>Sign up</h4>
        <p>Join the mailing list and we will email you before the fellowships begin.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>8 weekly sessions</h4>
        <p>
          A small group meets for 90 minutes each week. Sessions are taught, not just read:
          graduate students, PhD students and invited researchers lead them, followed by
          discussion.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Become a fellow</h4>
        <p>Finish the 8 weeks and you are a fellow, whichever track you took.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Get into research</h4>
        <p>
          Fellows get fellows-only research meetings and mixers with AI safety researchers at
          Northeastern and around Boston. We plan to work with Northeastern labs on projects
          fellows can join.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="actions section-actions">
      <Signup />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
